---
import MainLayout from '../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
import LegacyHeader from '../components/LegacyHeader.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import ContactSection from '../components/ContactSection.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import ButtonPrimary from '../components/ButtonPrimary.astro';
import ButtonSecondary from '../components/ButtonSecondary.astro';

const faqs = [
  {
    question: 'How is SaaS SEO different from other SEO?',
    answer: 'SaaS buyers research in stages — problem, solution, comparison, pricing — and each stage needs its own page type: use-case pages, feature pages, comparison and alternative pages, integrations, docs and a blog that does more than publish for the sake of it. SaaS SEO also has a longer feedback loop: the win is trial signups and demos, not one-off transactions. We build campaigns around that funnel rather than chasing raw traffic.'
  },
  {
    question: 'What results have you achieved for SaaS and software companies?',
    answer: 'Published examples: a football team management app grew organic clicks 34% in three months — from 200k to 268k, with average position improving from 11.4 to 9.1 into page-one territory. A fintech equity management SaaS grew AI referral sessions to 1,322 (+71.7% year over year) with visitors averaging over seven minutes on site. A sports SaaS grew AI referrals 405% to 4,549 sessions. All are published case studies with the data shown.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Does SEO make sense for SaaS when we already run paid acquisition?',
    answer: 'That is usually exactly when it makes sense. Paid CAC rises with competition and stops the moment budget stops; organic compounds. The strongest pattern we see is paid and organic working the same funnel: paid wins the head terms immediately while SEO builds durable rankings for comparison, use-case and problem searches — the queries where buyers make shortlists.'
  },
  {
    question: 'How important is AI search for SaaS companies?',
    answer: 'Critical, and it is already measurable. Software buyers increasingly ask ChatGPT and other assistants for tool recommendations. For a fintech SaaS client we tracked 1,322 LLM referral sessions in six months with every AI platform averaging over five minutes of engagement — high-intent visitors. For a sports SaaS we tracked 162 AI mentions and 239 AI link citations across five platforms. Being citable by AI is becoming part of how SaaS shortlists get made.'
  },
  {
    question: 'What is included in a SaaS SEO campaign?',
    answer: 'A defined monthly scope across six workstreams: technical SEO (crawlability, site speed, schema, docs and app-subdomain handling), keyword and funnel research, on-page optimisation, content production or briefs for comparison and use-case pages, authority building through relevant links and digital PR angles, and AI search optimisation. Reporting ties everything to signups and demo requests where tracking allows, not just rankings.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Do you write comparison and alternative pages?',
    answer: 'Yes — they are usually the highest-converting pages in SaaS SEO because they catch buyers at shortlist stage. We keep them honest: accurate feature comparisons, real differences acknowledged, no fabricated weaknesses in competitors. Honest comparison pages convert better anyway, because SaaS buyers can smell a hatchet job and they will verify claims in a free trial.'
  },
  {
    question: 'How long does SaaS SEO take to work?',
    answer: 'Expect three to six months for meaningful movement and six to twelve for the compounding effect that makes SEO cheaper than paid at scale. It can be faster when foundations exist: the football app campaign added 68k monthly clicks within a three-month comparison window. We set expectations against your starting authority, competition and content velocity — in writing, before you commit.'
  },
  {
    question: 'How much does SaaS SEO cost?',
    answer: 'Specialist SaaS SEO agencies in the US and UK typically charge the equivalent of $5,000 to $15,000+ a month. We deliver senior strategy and execution from the Philippines, which means the same scope costs meaningfully less — and more of the budget goes into content, technical work and links rather than agency overhead. Every campaign is scoped individually and quoted as a fixed monthly figure in writing.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Can you work with our product and engineering teams?',
    answer: 'Yes — SaaS SEO always touches product surfaces: docs, templates, programmatic pages, app subdomains, changelogs. Every technical recommendation ships with priority, impact and implementation notes engineers can act on, and we fit your sprint cadence rather than demanding our own. Where marketing owns the site, we can implement directly.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Do you understand product-led growth and freemium funnels?',
    answer: 'Yes. PLG changes what SEO should target: the goal is signups and activation, not enquiry forms, so content has to earn trust fast and route users into the product. Docs and help content become acquisition surfaces, templates and free tools become link magnets, and measurement has to follow users past the marketing site. We plan campaigns around your actual conversion path, whichever model you run.'
  },
  {
    question: 'Can you handle international SEO for SaaS?',
    answer: 'Yes. Software sells globally by default, and we run international campaigns daily — including hreflang architecture, market-specific content and country-relevant authority building. Our own case studies span the UK, Australia, New Zealand and international audiences, and one fintech client\'s AI referrals alone reached visitors from 80 countries.'
  }
];
---

<MainLayout
  title="SaaS SEO Agency | Organic Growth for Software | Bright Forge"
  description="SaaS SEO with published click growth and measured AI-search visits. Funnel pages, technical work and reporting. Send the product if trials are the goal."
  canonical="https://brightforge.com.ph/saas-seo-services/"
  type="service"
  faqs={faqs}
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
      '@context': 'https://schema.org',
      '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
      itemListElement: [
        { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://brightforge.com.ph/' },
        { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'SaaS SEO Services', item: 'https://brightforge.com.ph/saas-seo-services/' }
      ]
    })} />
  </Fragment>

  <LegacyHeader slot="header" />

  <Hero
    badgeIcon="fas fa-rocket"
    badgeText="SaaS SEO Specialists"
    title="SaaS SEO Services That Compound While <span>Your Paid CAC Keeps Climbing</span>"
    breadcrumbCurrent="SaaS SEO Services"
  >
    <Fragment slot="story">
      <p>Software buyers shortlist through search — Google today, and increasingly ChatGPT and AI assistants. We get SaaS products into those shortlists with funnel-led content, technical SEO and measured AI search visibility.</p>
      <p>The proof is published: we grew a football team management app's organic clicks 34% in three months to 268k a month, and we track AI referrals for SaaS clients down to the session — one fintech platform now earns 1,322 LLM referral sessions with seven-minute average engagement.</p>
      <p>Senior strategy, honest reporting, delivered from the Philippines at rates that leave budget for the work itself.</p>
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="actions">
      <ButtonPrimary href="/contact/" text="Get a SaaS SEO Proposal" />
      <ButtonSecondary href="#saas-results" text="See SaaS Results" />
    </Fragment>

    <Fragment slot="visual">
      <div class="market-visual" aria-label="SaaS SEO growth snapshot">
        <div class="market-node">
          <span>Sports app</span>
          <strong>200k → 268k monthly organic clicks in 3 months</strong>
        </div>
        <div class="market-line"></div>
        <div class="market-node forge">
          <span>Fintech SaaS</span>
          <strong>1,322 AI referral sessions, 7:11 avg engagement</strong>
        </div>
        <div class="market-line"></div>
        <div class="market-node">
          <span>Sports SaaS</span>
          <strong>+405% AI referrals, 239 AI citations tracked</strong>
        </div>
      </div>
    </Fragment>
  </Hero>

  <section class="proof-strip" aria-label="SaaS SEO proof points">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="proof-grid">
        <div><strong>68k extra monthly clicks</strong><span>Added for one app in 3 months</span></div>
        <div><strong>AI search measured</strong><span>Sessions, mentions and citations</span></div>
        <div><strong>Funnel-led content</strong><span>Comparison, use-case, docs</span></div>
        <div><strong>Engineering-friendly</strong><span>Specs your devs can ship</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section dark" id="who-for">
    <div class="container two-col">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Who this is for</p>
        <h2>A SaaS SEO agency for teams that need <span>pipeline, not just traffic</span></h2>
        <p class="lead">Traffic that does not sign up is a vanity metric. SaaS SEO succeeds when comparison-stage buyers find you, trust you and start a trial.</p>
        <p>We work with software companies at the stage where organic needs to start pulling its weight against paid — building the page types and authority that turn search demand into product signups.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="card-grid small">
        <article class="card"><h3>B2B SaaS</h3><p>Feature, use-case and comparison pages plus content that reaches decision-makers before your sales team does.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>PLG and freemium products</h3><p>SEO tuned for signups and activation — docs, templates and tools as acquisition surfaces.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Fintech and regulated software</h3><p>Authority-led SEO where trust signals and accuracy matter as much as rankings.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Apps and platforms</h3><p>Consumer and prosumer apps competing for high-volume search demand, like our <a href="/case-studies/football-app-seo/">football app client</a>.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section darker" id="saas-results">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head centered">
        <p class="eyebrow">Published SaaS results</p>
        <h2>Software SEO results <span>we show in public</span></h2>
        <p>Every card links to a full case study with the data on the page.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="results-grid">
        <article class="result-card">
          <p class="result-tag">Sports App · Team Management</p>
          <h3>+34% clicks: 200k → 268k a month</h3>
          <p>68k extra monthly organic clicks in a three-month comparison, with average position moving from 11.4 to 9.1 — into page-one territory.</p>
          <a href="/case-studies/football-app-seo/">Read the case study →</a>
        </article>
        <article class="result-card">
          <p class="result-tag">Fintech SaaS · AI Search</p>
          <h3>1,322 AI referral sessions, +71.7% YoY</h3>
          <p>An equity management platform whose AI-referred visitors average 7:11 on site — with referrals arriving from 80 countries.</p>
          <a href="/case-studies/ai-fintech-saas-geo/">Read the case study →</a>
        </article>
        <article class="result-card">
          <p class="result-tag">Sports SaaS · AI Search</p>
          <h3>+405% AI referrals to 4,549 sessions</h3>
          <p>162 AI mentions and 239 AI link citations tracked across five platforms — visibility where software shortlists now get made.</p>
          <a href="/case-studies/ai-sports-saas-geo/">Read the case study →</a>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section dark" id="services">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head centered">
        <p class="eyebrow">What we deliver</p>
        <h2>Full-funnel <span>SEO for software companies</span></h2>
        <p>Six workstreams, sequenced around your funnel and your sprint cadence — not a fixed monthly task list.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="service-grid">
        <article class="service-card"><i class="fas fa-filter"></i><h3>Funnel &amp; keyword research</h3><p>Problem, solution, comparison and pricing-stage demand mapped to the page types that convert each stage. See <a href="/keyword-research-services/">keyword research</a>.</p></article>
        <article class="service-card"><i class="fas fa-balance-scale"></i><h3>Comparison &amp; alternative pages</h3><p>Honest, accurate shortlist-stage pages — the highest-converting content in SaaS SEO.</p></article>
        <article class="service-card"><i class="fas fa-cogs"></i><h3>Technical SEO</h3><p>Crawlability, rendering, schema, docs and subdomain strategy via our <a href="/technical-seo-services-philippines/">technical SEO service</a> — specs your engineers can ship.</p></article>
        <article class="service-card"><i class="fas fa-pen-nib"></i><h3>Content production</h3><p>Use-case pages, integration pages and expert-led articles through our <a href="/content-seo-services-philippines/">content SEO service</a> — human-edited, never AI dumps.</p></article>
        <article class="service-card"><i class="fas fa-link"></i><h3>Authority building</h3><p>Relevant <a href="/backlink-seo-services-philippines/">link building</a> and digital PR angles that make sense for a software brand. No bulk packages.</p></article>
        <article class="service-card"><i class="fas fa-robot"></i><h3>AI search optimisation</h3><p>Entity clarity, citable content and measured LLM visibility through our <a href="/ai-search-optimization-services-philippines/">AI search service</a> — with published SaaS results.</p></article>
        <article class="service-card"><i class="fas fa-key"></i><h3>Competitor gap analysis</h3><p>Where rivals rank and you do not — and which gaps are worth closing first, by pipeline impact.</p></article>
        <article class="service-card"><i class="fas fa-chart-line"></i><h3>Signup-led reporting</h3><p>Monthly reports tied to GA4: clicks, signups and demo requests where tracked, work completed, next priorities.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section darker" id="ai-search">
    <div class="container two-col">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">The AI search shift</p>
        <h2>Software shortlists are moving to <span>ChatGPT — and we measure it</span></h2>
        <p class="lead">"Best tool for X" questions increasingly get asked to AI assistants instead of Google. Most agencies talk about this; we publish the numbers.</p>
        <p>Across our SaaS AI-search case studies (measured August 2025 to January 2026 with GA4, Search Console and SE Ranking): a fintech platform earning 1,322 LLM referral sessions with every AI platform averaging over five minutes of engagement, and a sports SaaS growing AI referrals 405% with 239 AI link citations tracked. The foundations are classic SEO — clear entities, strong authority, answer-ready pages — which is why AI search optimisation is built into every SaaS campaign we run, not sold as an upsell.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="timezone-card">
        <h3>What we track for AI visibility</h3>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>LLM referral sessions</strong> — actual visitors arriving from ChatGPT, Perplexity, Copilot and Gemini</li>
          <li><strong>Engagement quality</strong> — AI-referred SaaS visitors average 5+ minutes in our published data</li>
          <li><strong>Mentions and citations</strong> — where AI platforms name and link your product</li>
          <li><strong>Platform gaps</strong> — which assistants ignore you, and the content plan to fix it</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section dark" id="process">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-head centered">
        <p class="eyebrow">How a campaign runs</p>
        <h2>The first 90 days of a <span>SaaS SEO campaign</span></h2>
      </div>

      <div class="timeline">
        <article><span>Days 1–15</span><h3>Funnel diagnosis</h3><p>Technical audit, funnel-stage keyword mapping, competitor gaps and a priority plan tied to signups, not just traffic.</p></article>
        <article><span>Days 16–45</span><h3>Foundations</h3><p>Technical fixes shipped with your engineers, on-page work on money pages, and the comparison-page plan agreed.</p></article>
        <article><span>Days 46–75</span><h3>Content velocity</h3><p>Use-case, comparison and integration pages in production; authority building starts on the terms that matter.</p></article>
        <article><span>Days 76–90</span><h3>Measure and compound</h3><p>Review clicks, signups and AI visibility against the plan, then scale what the data supports.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section faq-section">
    <div class="container narrow">
      <div class="section-head centered">
        <p class="eyebrow">SaaS SEO FAQs</p>
        <h2><span>Questions software teams ask</span> before working with us</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="faq-list">
        {faqs.map((faq) => (
          <details class="faq-item">
            <summary>{faq.question}</summary>
            <p>{faq.answer}</p>
          </details>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="cta-section">
    <div class="container narrow cta-box">
      <p class="eyebrow">Ready to talk?</p>
      <h2>Get a straight answer about <span>SEO for your product</span></h2>
      <p>Tell us your product, your market and how you acquire users today. We will tell you honestly where organic can move pipeline — and how long it will realistically take — before any money changes hands.</p>
      <div class="cta-actions">
        <a href="/contact/" class="cta-primary">Get a SaaS SEO Proposal</a>
        <a href="/case-studies/" class="cta-secondary">View All Case Studies</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ContactSection slot="contact" />
  <Footer slot="footer" />
</MainLayout>

<style>
.container {
  width: min(1180px, calc(100% - 2rem));
  margin: 0 auto;
}

.narrow {
  width: min(900px, calc(100% - 2rem));
}

.market-visual {
  position: relative;
  display: grid;
  gap: 1.1rem;
  max-width: 480px;
  margin: 0 auto;
  padding: 1.5rem;
  border: 1px solid rgba(255, 107, 53, 0.25);
  border-radius: 28px;
  background: linear-gradient(145deg, rgba(19, 22, 39, 0.96), rgba(13, 15, 26, 0.92));
  box-shadow: 0 25px 80px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35);
}

.market-node {
  padding: 1.2rem;
  border-radius: 18px;
  background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06);
  border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
}

.market-node.forge {
  border-color: rgba(255, 107, 53, 0.35);
}

.market-node span {
  display: block;
  color: #ff8a5c;
  font-size: 0.82rem;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
}

.market-node strong {
  display: block;
  color: #fff;
  font-size: 1.05rem;
}

.market-line {
  height: 26px;
  width: 2px;
  background: linear-gradient(#ff6b35, transparent);
  margin-left: 1.2rem;
}

.proof-strip {
  background: #0d0f1a;
  border-top: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
  border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
  padding: 1.5rem 0;
}

.proof-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
  gap: 1rem;
}

.proof-grid div {
  padding: 1.1rem;
  border-radius: 16px;
  background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.045);
  border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
}

.proof-grid strong,
.proof-grid span {
  display: block;
}

.proof-grid strong {
  color: #fff;
  margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
}

.proof-grid span {
  color: #cfd3e6;
  font-size: 0.92rem;
}

.section {
  padding: 5.5rem 0;
}

.dark {
  background: #131627;
}

.darker {
  background: #0d0f1a;
}

.two-col {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.9fr) minmax(0, 1.1fr);
  gap: 3rem;
  align-items: center;
}

.eyebrow {
  color: #ff8a5c;
  font-weight: 700;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.1em;
  font-size: 0.82rem;
  margin-bottom: 0.85rem;
}

h2 {
  color: #fff;
  font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.2rem);
  line-height: 1.05;
  margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
}

h3 {
  color: #fff;
  font-size: 1.2rem;
  margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
}

p,
li {
  color: #d0d4e8;
  line-height: 1.75;
}

.lead {
  font-size: 1.15rem;
  color: #e4e7f5;
}

.section-head {
  max-width: 820px;
  margin-bottom: 3rem;
}

.centered {
  text-align: center;
  margin-left: auto;
  margin-right: auto;
}

.card-grid,
.service-grid,
.results-grid,
.timeline {
  display: grid;
  gap: 1.25rem;
}

.card-grid.small {
  grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
}

.card,
.service-card,
.result-card,
.timezone-card,
.timeline article,
.faq-item {
  background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.055);
  border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
  border-radius: 22px;
  padding: 1.5rem;
}

.card a,
.service-card a {
  color: #ff8a5c;
}

.service-grid {
  grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
}

.service-card i {
  display: inline-grid;
  place-items: center;
  width: 46px;
  height: 46px;
  margin-bottom: 1rem;
  border-radius: 14px;
  color: #fff;
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ff6b35, #ff9f1c);
}

.results-grid {
  grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
}

.result-tag {
  color: #ff8a5c;
  font-size: 0.82rem;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
}

.result-card a {
  display: inline-block;
  margin-top: 0.75rem;
  color: #ff8a5c;
  font-weight: 700;
  text-decoration: none;
}

.timeline {
  grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);
}

.timeline span {
  display: inline-block;
  color: #ff8a5c;
  font-weight: 800;
  margin-bottom: 0.9rem;
}

.timezone-card {
  background: linear-gradient(145deg, rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08), rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.035));
}

.timezone-card ul {
  list-style: none;
  padding: 0;
  margin: 1.25rem 0 0;
}

.timezone-card li {
  position: relative;
  padding-left: 1.75rem;
  margin-bottom: 0.8rem;
}

.timezone-card li::before {
  content: '✓';
  position: absolute;
  left: 0;
  color: #ff8a5c;
  font-weight: 800;
}

.faq-section {
  background: #131627;
}

.faq-list {
  display: grid;
  gap: 1rem;
}

.faq-item summary {
  cursor: pointer;
  color: #fff;
  font-weight: 700;
  font-size: 1.08rem;
}

.faq-item p {
  margin-top: 1rem;
}

.cta-section {
  padding: 5rem 0;
  background: #0d0f1a;
}

.cta-box {
  text-align: center;
  padding: 3rem;
  border-radius: 28px;
  background: linear-gradient(135deg, rgba(255, 107, 53, 0.18), rgba(255, 159, 28, 0.08));
  border: 1px solid rgba(255, 107, 53, 0.28);
}

.cta-actions {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: center;
  flex-wrap: wrap;
  gap: 1rem;
  margin-top: 2rem;
}

.cta-primary,
.cta-secondary {
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  min-height: 48px;
  padding: 0.85rem 1.4rem;
  border-radius: 999px;
  font-weight: 800;
  text-decoration: none;
}

.cta-primary {
  color: #0d0f1a;
  background: #fff;
}

.cta-secondary {
  color: #fff;
  border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.35);
}

@media (max-width: 980px) {
  .proof-grid,
  .service-grid,
  .timeline {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
  }

  .results-grid {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }

  .two-col {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }
}

@media (max-width: 640px) {
  .section {
    padding: 4rem 0;
  }

  .proof-grid,
  .service-grid,
  .timeline,
  .card-grid.small {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
  }

  .cta-box {
    padding: 2rem 1.25rem;
  }
}
</style>
